      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224244/assets/7a1491a141cde19434464ee6ca7c57a5214aa75ddf26e189bb05b756a68b96da.png)\n\nWhich of the following is a polyhedron with exactly $4$ faces?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine the solids one-by-one.\n\n- I  is a polyhedron and it has exactly $6$ faces.\n\n- II  is a polyhedron and it has exactly $5$ faces.\n\n- III is a polyhedron but it has exactly $4$ faces.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"III only\".",
